Omarchy Quick Share includes a modified rquickshare core.

Original project: rquickshare by Martichou and its contributors.
Source: https://github.com/Martichou/rquickshare
Imported revision: 378d8ae969941bee4bf60ad34ac9cf8bb7005eb7
Original license: GNU General Public License version 3, supplied in LICENSE.

Modified for Omarchy Quick Share on 2026-10-09:
- Replaced duplicate TCP-only handlers with a shared encrypted session.
- Added Bluetooth discovery and RFCOMM streams, transport negotiation,
  NetworkManager hotspot handling, consent and crash-state recovery.
- Added bounded framing, authenticated message checks, safe staged file
  publication, cancellation and transport/error events.
- Removed the obsolete TypeScript export layer and standalone core binary.
- Pinned mdns-sd to the exact Cargo.lock revision for reproducible builds.
- Since 0.3.5, use the locally vendored mdns-sd security fork based on that
  revision, with intrinsic DNS parser/cache and derived-state budgets.
  Its provenance and modification notice are in ../mdns-sd/NOTICE.

The Google-origin protobuf schemas preserve their Apache-2.0 headers.
The modified offline_wire_formats.proto carries a change notice; the full
license is supplied in LICENSE-APACHE. wire_format.proto instead preserves
Copyright 2020 The Chromium Authors and its BSD-style header. Its license
is supplied separately in LICENSE-CHROMIUM, obtained from the Chromium
upstream LICENSE: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/chromium/chromium/main/LICENSE
The schema itself is pinned by the imported rquickshare revision above.
The modern IntroductionFrame metadata and ProgressUpdateFrame additions
to wire_format.proto originate from Copyright 2023 Google LLC,
Apache-2.0, supplied in LICENSE-APACHE. Source pinned at:
https://github.com/google/nearby/blob/d128b5fca30b3fa8d4642f8c75dd9e314e090e74/sharing/proto/wire_format.proto
The BandwidthUpgradeRetryFrame addition to offline_wire_formats.proto
is from the same Google revision (Apache-2.0):
https://github.com/google/nearby/blob/d128b5fca30b3fa8d4642f8c75dd9e314e090e74/connections/implementation/proto/offline_wire_formats.proto


Protocol references include Google Nearby Connections (Apache-2.0):
https://github.com/google/nearby
